01:38:19.380 --> 01:38:21.087
like a show that's a bit different,

01:38:21.087 --> 01:38:24.187
but at the same time he
used every trope combined,

01:38:24.187 --> 01:38:25.725
like, yeah, whatever-

01:38:25.725 --> 01:38:27.443
- That's the weird thing
about a lot of anime.

01:38:27.443 --> 01:38:31.740
It is the most tropey unique
shows that for some reason,

01:38:31.740 --> 01:38:32.840
get the most attention.

01:38:32.840 --> 01:38:33.920
It's like, you look at it,

01:38:33.920 --> 01:38:35.495
like someone will look at it and be like,

01:38:35.495 --> 01:38:36.753
like Eva, for instance, right?

01:38:36.753 --> 01:38:37.950
Someone will look at Eva and being like,

01:38:37.950 --> 01:38:40.790
"Whoa, I've never seen
anything like this at all."

01:38:40.790 --> 01:38:41.960
But at the same time,

01:38:41.960 --> 01:38:43.530
it's the type of show where
another person will look at it

01:38:43.530 --> 01:38:46.550
and be like, this has every
trope that I've ever seen.

01:38:46.550 --> 01:38:48.336
- Dude, "One Punch Man."

01:38:48.336 --> 01:38:49.503
- Yeah.
- Okay?

01:38:52.499 --> 01:38:55.690
My cousin's kids a
couple of Christmases ago

01:38:55.690 --> 01:38:58.273
when I went back and they've
started talking about,

01:38:58.273 --> 01:38:59.927
"Oh yeah, we watched this
thing, "One Punch Man."

01:38:59.927 --> 01:39:01.120
It's really cool."

01:39:01.120 --> 01:39:03.340
And I blew their minds by going,

01:39:03.340 --> 01:39:04.835
"This is actually based on

01:39:04.835 --> 01:39:07.385
a little kid's TV show
called 'Wanpanman.'"

01:39:07.385 --> 01:39:08.410
(all laughing)

01:39:08.410 --> 01:39:10.460
And that character is based on like

01:39:10.460 --> 01:39:12.120
the "Dragonball" character,
this one and this,

01:39:12.120 --> 01:39:13.930
it was actually voiced by the same guy-

01:39:13.930 --> 01:39:15.760
- You dropped the anime knowledge on them.

01:39:15.760 --> 01:39:16.751
- I just, I explained-

01:39:16.751 --> 01:39:18.024
- Man, Mr Worldwide over there.

01:39:18.024 --> 01:39:19.590
- You fucking schooled them, man.

01:39:19.590 --> 01:39:22.198
- So everything you like is actually based

01:39:22.198 --> 01:39:23.381
on something else.

01:39:23.381 --> 01:39:24.747
(all laughing)

01:39:24.747 --> 01:39:26.450
- Your life is a lie, don't be happy

01:39:26.450 --> 01:39:27.720
and I'll tell you why.

01:39:27.720 --> 01:39:29.687
- That's exactly what I
was aiming to destroy them

01:39:29.687 --> 01:39:31.218
'cause, yeah, it was just fun.

01:39:31.218 --> 01:39:32.900
- Not gonna lie, doing that is fun.

01:39:32.900 --> 01:39:34.507
- Destroying them with facts and history.

01:39:34.507 --> 01:39:36.004
- See, that's what this is.

01:39:36.004 --> 01:39:37.169
And so you actually like this,

01:39:37.169 --> 01:39:38.002
you should actually like this.

01:39:38.002 --> 01:39:39.113
But again, it's a gateway thing.

01:39:39.113 --> 01:39:40.511
Hey, anything that gets people into it,

01:39:40.511 --> 01:39:43.413
it's like, look, I
don't, who cares anymore?

01:39:43.413 --> 01:39:46.234
Like, "Oh, you're a bunch of
normie fans, what do you know?"

01:39:46.234 --> 01:39:49.950
It's like, no, you start
somewhere, you go this far.

01:39:49.950 --> 01:39:52.570
It's like the same thing
you guys have done drifting.

01:39:52.570 --> 01:39:54.172
If you don't want to go any further,

01:39:54.172 --> 01:39:55.609
it's like, well, why would you?

01:39:55.609 --> 01:39:57.430
Like if you don't understand
enough, that's fine.

01:39:57.430 --> 01:39:58.338
You enjoyed it.

01:39:58.338 --> 01:40:00.780
It was like you got your adrenaline hit,

01:40:00.780 --> 01:40:02.894
and it was some weird stuff
you've never done before.

01:40:02.894 --> 01:40:05.987
You have a new experience that
you've done, it's in Japan.

01:40:05.987 --> 01:40:08.090
You've done drifting in Japan.

01:40:08.090 --> 01:40:10.581
Like that was, I guess this
is the thing that I have

01:40:10.581 --> 01:40:12.312
to offer to other people.

01:40:12.312 --> 01:40:14.710
And I always try and not force it on them,

01:40:14.710 --> 01:40:16.020
but if I can, at some opportunity,

01:40:16.020 --> 01:40:18.044
like for example,

01:40:18.044 --> 01:40:20.740
when Reckful and Sodapoppin came to Japan

01:40:20.740 --> 01:40:25.633
for their legendary stream
on Twitch, their IRL stream,

01:40:25.633 --> 01:40:27.760
I hunted them down and said,

01:40:27.760 --> 01:40:29.600
"You have to come and go drifting."

01:40:29.600 --> 01:40:33.370
'Cause Team Orange had
two of their drift cars

01:40:33.370 --> 01:40:35.756
at a dive bar, which is only about-

01:40:35.756 --> 01:40:37.627
- Very close to Central Tokyo.

01:40:37.627 --> 01:40:40.612
- Yeah, less than an hour
from anywhere in Tokyo

01:40:40.612 --> 01:40:41.686
to go drifting.

01:40:41.686 --> 01:40:42.880
So, 'cause I know them, I hooked it up.

01:40:42.880 --> 01:40:44.006
I said, "Yeah, come
here, we'll meet here."

01:40:44.006 --> 01:40:45.514
We take them, sent them drifting.

01:40:45.514 --> 01:40:46.702
They went out that night

01:40:46.702 --> 01:40:49.284
and did Ram and Rem cosplay
play on the streets.

01:40:49.284 --> 01:40:50.274
(all laughing)

01:40:50.274 --> 01:40:51.807
So I guess they had a good day.

01:40:51.807 --> 01:40:52.692
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:40:52.692 --> 01:40:55.253
- Other guys like, the
IRL stream of JakeNBake,

01:40:55.253 --> 01:40:56.557
the Japanese IRL stream.

01:40:56.557 --> 01:40:59.890
I got him a ride in a D1 Grand Prix car,

01:41:01.230 --> 01:41:05.148
it was about maybe 1200 horsepower GTR,

01:41:05.148 --> 01:41:07.014
live streaming it to like whatever it was,

01:41:07.014 --> 01:41:10.137
like 20,000, 12,000, whatever people.

01:41:10.137 --> 01:41:12.767
I love to, if I can just
present it to people as like,

01:41:12.767 --> 01:41:14.140
'cause I honestly,

01:41:14.140 --> 01:41:17.800
I think it is a really good
part of Japanese culture

01:41:17.800 --> 01:41:21.050
that is not only fun and relatable but,

01:41:21.961 --> 01:41:23.570
I mean any, like you said,

01:41:23.570 --> 01:41:26.536
you know it because of "Fast and Furious",

01:41:26.536 --> 01:41:28.316
people saying "Initial D"

01:41:28.316 --> 01:41:30.157
and I think it's a cool thing

01:41:30.157 --> 01:41:32.670
that I like people to
experience and I enjoy it.

01:41:32.670 --> 01:41:33.834
- They're super welcoming as well.

01:41:33.834 --> 01:41:34.808
- Yeah, yeah.

01:41:34.808 --> 01:41:36.520
- They were really friendly
to us at the track.

01:41:36.520 --> 01:41:38.927
- Now, if only every
community was like that.

01:41:38.927 --> 01:41:39.994
(all laughing)

01:41:39.994 --> 01:41:41.440
- Oh, go ahead.
- Go ahead.

01:41:41.440 --> 01:41:42.382
- Okay no, 'cause I was going to say,

01:41:42.382 --> 01:41:45.330
I mean, like you talked about
getting people to experience

01:41:45.330 --> 01:41:46.382
this for the first time.

01:41:46.382 --> 01:41:48.965
I'm sure we've done that
like introducing our friends

01:41:48.965 --> 01:41:50.630
and everything into anime

01:41:50.630 --> 01:41:52.630
where we can just like
recommend a show or something.

01:41:52.630 --> 01:41:55.340
But I feel like it's
infinitely harder with drifting

01:41:55.340 --> 01:41:57.084
because like, as we've talked about,

01:41:57.084 --> 01:41:59.730
the barrier of entry is like so high.

01:41:59.730 --> 01:42:02.435
And I feel like it's one of those hobbies

01:42:02.435 --> 01:42:05.373
where no one just casually
drift, you know what I mean?

01:42:05.373 --> 01:42:06.320
(all laughing)

01:42:06.320 --> 01:42:07.662
You can't just be a casual drifter.

01:42:07.662 --> 01:42:10.613
You like either in this all the way,

01:42:10.613 --> 01:42:13.158
or like, it's something
you experienced once

01:42:13.158 --> 01:42:16.017
and you know, I would
love to go drifting more.

01:42:16.017 --> 01:42:18.517
It was a fucking hell of an experience,

01:42:18.517 --> 01:42:19.966
but at the same time, it's like,

01:42:19.966 --> 01:42:22.697
"Do I have the time and the
money to commit to this?"

01:42:22.697 --> 01:42:24.768
And it's something-

01:42:24.768 --> 01:42:26.585
- Just quit gacha.

01:42:26.585 --> 01:42:29.328
He said he spent like 30K, we said?

01:42:29.328 --> 01:42:30.870
- That's a minimum.

01:42:30.870 --> 01:42:32.856
- That's probably
Garnt's monthly allowance

01:42:32.856 --> 01:42:34.920
on gacha, come on.

01:42:34.920 --> 01:42:35.878
Quit gacha.

01:42:35.878 --> 01:42:38.145
- He was telling me on the
train here that he's like, "Man,

01:42:38.145 --> 01:42:39.760
I would go drifting.

01:42:39.760 --> 01:42:41.310
I just have to quit gacha."

01:42:41.310 --> 01:42:43.172
(all laughing)

01:42:43.172 --> 01:42:45.220
"But it's so hard."

01:42:45.220 --> 01:42:46.937
- I think one thing
that I really appreciate

01:42:46.937 --> 01:42:48.757
about your channel in particular,

01:42:48.757 --> 01:42:50.493
and to anyone listening,

01:42:50.493 --> 01:42:53.410
that whereas a lot of YouTubers here

01:42:53.410 --> 01:42:54.893
who live in Japan who are foreign,

01:42:54.893 --> 01:42:56.412
it feels like an outsider looking in

01:42:56.412 --> 01:42:57.606
on a lot of the content.

01:42:57.606 --> 01:42:59.338
And what was really refreshing
I think from your videos,

01:42:59.338 --> 01:43:02.827
what I got was that it was
like you were in it with them

01:43:02.827 --> 01:43:05.729
and that you knew all the
big players in the scene.

01:43:05.729 --> 01:43:07.380
It was really cool seeing that aspect

01:43:07.380 --> 01:43:09.102
'cause I thought, when I
first watched your video,

01:43:09.102 --> 01:43:10.435
that it was gonna be like,

01:43:10.435 --> 01:43:12.310
"Hey, I'm here, let's
find out what's going on.

01:43:12.310 --> 01:43:13.143
I'm gonna see what's happening."

01:43:13.143 --> 01:43:14.985
But you were like saying hi to
everyone, everyone knew you.

01:43:14.985 --> 01:43:16.215
It was so cool.

01:43:16.215 --> 01:43:17.228
- I roll deep.

01:43:17.228 --> 01:43:20.131
- Yeah, it was really cool seeing that,

01:43:20.131 --> 01:43:23.268
you get a YouTuber in Japan
who is really deep in the scene

01:43:23.268 --> 01:43:25.397
to the point of where even the people

01:43:25.397 --> 01:43:27.337
in the Japanese scene would know you.

01:43:27.337 --> 01:43:28.730
It's really cool seeing that.

01:43:28.730 --> 01:43:30.388
- That mostly came from the
fact that back in the day

01:43:30.388 --> 01:43:32.170
when I was doing, journalist work-

01:43:32.170 --> 01:43:33.842
- You've been around so long.

01:43:33.842 --> 01:43:36.674
- Well, it's like, if I want
to get access to cool stuff,

01:43:36.674 --> 01:43:38.664
I have to make friends.
- [Connor] Make friends.

01:43:38.664 --> 01:43:39.863
- I have to get to known to people

01:43:39.863 --> 01:43:41.057
and have to show them.

01:43:41.057 --> 01:43:43.316
You know, I would, any
event I would show up.

01:43:43.316 --> 01:43:46.104
This is the thing about
anything about Japan,

01:43:46.104 --> 01:43:47.828
especially is show up.

01:43:47.828 --> 01:43:50.159
Obviously right now you
can't really do that.

01:43:50.159 --> 01:43:52.550
But if you want to be
in something, show up,

01:43:52.550 --> 01:43:54.812
talk to people, get to know people.

01:43:54.812 --> 01:43:57.120
I mean, I've been on tours of,

01:43:57.120 --> 01:43:59.223
like a couple of anime
studios because I'm friends

01:43:59.223 --> 01:44:00.750
with someone else who knows someone else.

01:44:00.750 --> 01:44:02.987
And you just because you know someone

01:44:02.987 --> 01:44:04.199
and "Oh, Alexi's into that stuff.

01:44:04.199 --> 01:44:05.032
Why don't we go?

01:44:05.032 --> 01:44:05.865
Do you want to come too?

01:44:05.865 --> 01:44:07.240
We're doing something."

01:44:07.240 --> 01:44:08.680
It's just knowing people and yeah.

01:44:08.680 --> 01:44:10.752
Eventually it gets to a
tipping point where it's like

01:44:10.752 --> 01:44:13.162
you show up and like,
"Oh yeah, there's Alexi."

01:44:13.162 --> 01:44:16.048
That's why my friends told me,
like when I first got here,

01:44:16.048 --> 01:44:20.000
it's like it's very difficult
for a Japanese person

01:44:20.000 --> 01:44:22.363
to get to know and trust a foreigner

01:44:22.363 --> 01:44:25.268
because they just assume
that you're not gonna be here

01:44:25.268 --> 01:44:26.388
in a year or so.

01:44:26.388 --> 01:44:28.557
And another person told me too like,

01:44:28.557 --> 01:44:30.620
"Alexi, you have to keep
going to track days again,

01:44:30.620 --> 01:44:31.670
like all the time.

01:44:31.670 --> 01:44:32.754
Because if you don't,

01:44:32.754 --> 01:44:35.230
people just gonna forget
about you, straight away."

01:44:35.230 --> 01:44:37.413
So I do make an effort
to, even if I don't,

01:44:37.413 --> 01:44:38.790
even if I'm not driving,

01:44:38.790 --> 01:44:40.787
like I got today off,
I'll go to the track.

01:44:40.787 --> 01:44:43.041
Maybe I'll make a, I'll
take my equipment with me,

01:44:43.041 --> 01:44:44.417
maybe if there's something
cool, I'll make a video.

01:44:44.417 --> 01:44:46.585
But otherwise I'll just hang
around and talk to people

01:44:46.585 --> 01:44:48.130
and walk through the pits

01:44:48.130 --> 01:44:48.963
and everyone "Morning, morning."

01:44:48.963 --> 01:44:50.642
(speaking in foreign language)

01:44:50.642 --> 01:44:53.804
And then eventually they'll come to you,

01:44:53.804 --> 01:44:55.857
"Oh Alexi, (speaking in foreign language)"

01:44:55.857 --> 01:44:57.654
and they'll have something
cool and someone will be like,

01:44:57.654 --> 01:44:59.100
"Oh, are you driving today?"

01:44:59.100 --> 01:45:00.675
Ah, no, I just turned up.

01:45:00.675 --> 01:45:02.708
"Oh, you wanna take my car
out for a couple of laps?"

01:45:02.708 --> 01:45:04.607
I'm like hell yeah.

01:45:04.607 --> 01:45:06.754
I've got my helmet in the van.

01:45:06.754 --> 01:45:08.960
I'll bring my helmet with me just in case.

01:45:08.960 --> 01:45:10.736
- Take the shirt off like the whole team.

01:45:10.736 --> 01:45:11.815
- I'm ready.

01:45:11.815 --> 01:45:13.323
- Got my race suit on.

01:45:13.323 --> 01:45:14.727
(all laughing)

01:45:14.727 --> 01:45:16.311
Yeah, it's just show up and do it.

01:45:16.311 --> 01:45:17.208
And it gets like that after a while.

01:45:17.208 --> 01:45:19.205
I mean, I've been here 12 years, so,

01:45:19.205 --> 01:45:21.268
and I've been coming here
for longer than that too.

01:45:21.268 --> 01:45:23.830
- I think that kind of applies
with any social situation.

01:45:23.830 --> 01:45:25.080
- [Alexi] Absolutely.

01:45:25.080 --> 01:45:27.066
- It's like, it's just
about commitment, right?

01:45:27.066 --> 01:45:27.908
Like you just got to,

01:45:27.908 --> 01:45:29.774
if you want to be known in that circle

01:45:29.774 --> 01:45:31.526
or you want to be part of that circle,

01:45:31.526 --> 01:45:32.986
whatever that circle might be

01:45:32.986 --> 01:45:34.690
or whatever that niche might be,

01:45:34.690 --> 01:45:37.440
if you don't make an effort
to want to actually show,

01:45:37.440 --> 01:45:40.748
your commitment to it or
want to be like part of it,

01:45:40.748 --> 01:45:42.514
then you're not gonna get in.

01:45:42.514 --> 01:45:43.480
- Right.
- Yeah.

01:45:43.480 --> 01:45:46.060
- I was gonna say like it's the same thing

01:45:46.060 --> 01:45:48.649
with like the anime industry as well.

01:45:48.649 --> 01:45:50.779
Like once you know a couple of people,

01:45:50.779 --> 01:45:52.222
it's such a small industry

01:45:52.222 --> 01:45:54.442
that your face just gets known everywhere

01:45:54.442 --> 01:45:56.201
as long as you're staying committed to it.

01:45:56.201 --> 01:45:57.780
Like, that's really the only reason why

01:45:57.780 --> 01:45:59.221
like any of us have like-

01:45:59.221 --> 01:46:00.673
- That's just like our friend Nabi

01:46:00.673 --> 01:46:01.713
in like a nutshell, right?

01:46:01.713 --> 01:46:02.546
- Yeah, exactly.

01:46:02.546 --> 01:46:03.912
- Like he just seems to know everyone.

01:46:03.912 --> 01:46:06.013
And when I ask him,
it's just, he just says,

01:46:06.013 --> 01:46:08.541
"Oh, you know, I just know
a guy, who knows a guy who,

01:46:08.541 --> 01:46:09.374
I've just been around enough."

01:46:09.374 --> 01:46:12.698
- I just go around and
just make myself known.

01:46:12.698 --> 01:46:14.654
That's so, but the thing is

01:46:14.654 --> 01:46:17.953
that's like so much easier said than done.

01:46:17.953 --> 01:46:20.314
Because it is a lot of
commitment and it does take time

01:46:20.314 --> 01:46:22.804
and it's not guaranteed either

01:46:22.804 --> 01:46:23.860
that you're gonna get results.

01:46:23.860 --> 01:46:26.368
- No, it's just you got to build up

01:46:26.368 --> 01:46:27.378
recognition and everything.

01:46:27.378 --> 01:46:30.466
'Cause it was interesting
you mentioned a point that

01:46:30.466 --> 01:46:32.612
people in Japan just
assume people are gonna

01:46:32.612 --> 01:46:36.503
to be living here, like unpermanently.

01:46:36.503 --> 01:46:40.063
'Cause having lived abroad
in a few different countries,

01:46:40.063 --> 01:46:44.414
there's like you make some
expat friends sometimes, right?

01:46:44.414 --> 01:46:47.464
Who you can be like the
closest friends with them

01:46:47.464 --> 01:46:48.413
for like a few years,

01:46:48.413 --> 01:46:50.704
but then eventually
they're gonna move back.

01:46:50.704 --> 01:46:52.641
And it's really hard building up

01:46:52.641 --> 01:46:54.773
a friendship from zero again,

01:46:54.773 --> 01:46:57.964
when you knowsometimes that
people aren't gonna to be here

01:46:57.964 --> 01:46:59.266
in like two or three years.

01:46:59.266 --> 01:47:00.668
- Yeah, I've definitely noticed that,

01:47:00.668 --> 01:47:02.029
that I even I made some
friends who had just moved here

01:47:02.029 --> 01:47:04.109
and I'm like, "Oh cool,
I'm making friends."

01:47:04.109 --> 01:47:05.317
And then they left.

01:47:05.317 --> 01:47:06.306
(Joey laughs)

01:47:06.306 --> 01:47:07.244
I was like damn,

01:47:07.244 --> 01:47:09.284
finally started getting some
good list of friends going

01:47:09.284 --> 01:47:10.454
and they all just fucking left.

01:47:10.454 --> 01:47:11.300
- Yeah.
- They just yeeted out.

01:47:11.300 --> 01:47:13.179
- Can you imagine they
had their own problems?

01:47:13.179 --> 01:47:14.471
(Garnt laughing)

01:47:14.471 --> 01:47:15.588
- How dare they?

01:47:15.588 --> 01:47:17.935
- I know.
- The audacity.

01:47:17.935 --> 01:47:18.954
- The audacity.

01:47:18.954 --> 01:47:21.549
- The audacity to have nationalities aside

01:47:21.549 --> 01:47:23.855
from the place I'm living
right at this moment.

01:47:23.855 --> 01:47:26.729
- I have to ask because
you've seen our drift special,

01:47:26.729 --> 01:47:28.089
who was the best drifter?

01:47:28.089 --> 01:47:28.974
